    {
      "title": "Indian national killed, 2 hurt in attack on Saudi Arabia's Dammam airport",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/indian-national-killed-2-hurt-in-attack-on-saudi-arabia-s-dammam-airport-126102200643_1.html",
      "description": "An Indian national was killed and two others were injured in an attack on Dammam airport in Saudi Arabia, officials said on Thursday, a day after another compatriot was injured in a drone attack targeting the kingdom's Shaybah oilfield, amid a spate of strikes by Yemen's Houthi rebels on key infrastructure in the country.\nThe Indian Embassy in Riyadh said Saudi authorities have informed it about the casualties in the attack on Wednesday night.\n\"One Indian national was among two people who unfortunately lost their lives in the attack on Dammam airport yesterday night and two Indian nationals were injured,\" the embassy said in a social media post.\nThe mission said it is ascertaining further details and contacting the affected families.\n\"Our thoughts and prayers are with the family and loved ones of the deceased and we wish speedy recovery of the injured,\" it said.\nThe attack comes amid escalating drone and missile strikes targeting Saudi Arabia's airports, energy installations and o",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-22T09:08:28"
    },
    {
      "title": "Saudi Arabia seeks access to foreign strategic oil reserves for Aramco",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/saudi-arabia-seeks-access-to-foreign-strategic-oil-reserves-for-aramco-126102200679_1.html",
      "description": "Aramco CEO Amin Nasser said Saudi Arabia's Energy Ministry is discussing access to government-held oil storage abroad as Houthi attacks on key infrastructure raise concerns over supply disruptions",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-22T08:55:03"
    },
    {
      "title": "One killed, 8 injured in attack on Saudi Arabia's King Fahd airport",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/one-killed-8-injured-in-attack-on-saudi-arabia-s-king-fahd-airport-126102200050_1.html",
      "description": "One Saudi resident was killed in an attack on King Fahd International airport in Dammam in eastern Saudi Arabia on the Persian Gulf near Bahrain and Qatar, the Saudi Civil Aviation Authority announced early on Thursday.\nThe Civil Aviation authority also said eight people were injured in the late Wednesday attack and the airport suffered some material damages. Global flight-tracking service Flightradar24 said overnight Thursday on X that flights have been diverted away from the airport.\nKing Fahd airport has been attacked previously amid a wider wave of Houthi missile and projectile strikes targeting major airports in Saudi Arabia.\nThe Iranian-backed Houthis have not commented on this attack. The Saudi Coalition announced that it intercepted four drone attacks in the Eastern region.\nThe attack comes after Saudi Arabia's Energy Ministry said that debris from an intercepted drone killed two people and injured two others at an Aramco-operated oil field in the country's southeast.\nThe",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-22T02:39:02"
    },
